WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.950
Television is supposed to be entertainment.

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:08.760
And it's pretty deliciously entertaining when
TV writers try to predict the future.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:14.780
Sometimes they don't even mean to, but TV
shows have called out world events long before

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:15.920
they've happened.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.369
Here are eerie examples of some silly little
TV shows that somehow knew what was going

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:24.220
to happen before the rest of us...

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:26.909
Chris Rock knew O.J. did it...Before O.J.

00:00:26.909 --> 00:00:27.909
Did

00:00:27.909 --> 00:00:33.160
In the first moments of the very first episode
of The Chris Rock Show on HBO, Rock aired

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:39.379
a sketch about O.J. Simpson hawking a videotape
called "I Didn't Kill My Wife, But If I Did,

00:00:39.379 --> 00:00:40.579
Here's How I'd Do It."

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:46.059
It brutally mocked Simpson, acquitted for
the murder of his ex-wife in 1995, but still

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:49.280
widely believed by the public to be guilty.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:55.449
Amazingly, almost ten years later, Simpson
imitated that sketch in real life, with an

00:00:55.449 --> 00:00:59.929
almost exact same title, when he penned his
book, If I Did It.

00:00:59.929 --> 00:01:06.100
To promote it, he even taped a TV special
called If I Did It, Here's How it Happened.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:11.000
Ultimately, good taste prevailed, and neither
were released.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.240
Family Guy Predicts Caitlyn Jenner

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:18.880
In a brief, throwaway gag in an episode from
2009, baby Stewie Griffin casually tells Brian

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.689
the dog the truth about Bruce Jenner.

00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:23.579
"Bruce Jenner is a woman.

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:26.450
An elegant, beautiful Dutch woman."

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:31.170
That was a full six years before Jenner announced
that she now identifies as a woman and goes

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.509
by Caitlyn Jenner.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:35.820
As far as we know, she still isn't Dutch.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:38.150
An X-Files Spinoff Envisions 9/11

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:44.560
In 2001, the conspiracy theorist characters
from The X-Files known as the Lone Gunmen

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.009
got their own short-lived series.

00:01:47.009 --> 00:01:51.899
On the first episode, they uncovered a conspiracy
about the U.S. government planning to crash

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:57.469
an airplane into the World Trade Center, blame
it on foreigners, and then use the resultant

00:01:57.469 --> 00:02:01.180
outcry to justify raising the defense budget.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:05.750
Apart from real-life conspiracy theorists
who believe the U.S. government was behind

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.989
the events of 9/11, it’s chilling that a
TV show suggested the possibility of an airplane

00:02:10.989 --> 00:02:16.040
flying into the Twin Towers only months before
it actually occurred.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.110
Quantum Leap And The 1996 Super Bowl

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:24.580
In a 1990 episode of Quantum Leap, Sam quantum
leaped into the body of a high school football

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:25.580
player.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:30.629
In keeping with the football theme of the
episode, Sam's holographic advisor Al mentions

00:02:30.629 --> 00:02:34.319
that he's watching the tail end of the 1996
Super Bowl.

00:02:34.319 --> 00:02:36.450
"I been watching Super Bowl 30.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.730
Oh Sam the Steelers are down by 3 you wouldn't
believe-"

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.890
"Al this is the only game I care about."

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:46.239
That’s really how Super Bowl 30 in 1996
went down.

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:51.150
The Pittsburgh Steelers were in the game against
the Dallas Cowboys, and in the fourth quarter,

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:54.030
the team really was down by 3.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.950
"Oh boy"

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:58.280
The Simpsons Called It: President Trump

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:03.200
The Simpsons has a lot of episodes set in
the future, but they’re usually just a vehicle

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.430
to make jokes about future technology.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:10.160
For example, in an episode where Lisa is in
college, robots are common but they catch

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.580
fire and melt whenever they feel human emotion.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.409
In the same episode, Lisa calls Marge with
video-phone technology.

00:03:17.409 --> 00:03:22.340
And whilst we do have Skype and FaceTime,
we're still waiting for our melting robots.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:27.819
So take what you will from this prediction,
first aired way back in 2000, when Lisa gets

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:28.819
elected president:

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:32.850
"As you know we've inherited quite a budget
crunch from President Trump."

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:33.850
It's possible!

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:38.370
After all, The Simpsons has correctly predicted
the actual outcomes of elections before...

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:39.370
"America!

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.930
Take a good look at your beloved candidates!

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:45.010
They're nothing but hideous space reptiles!"

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:50.610
(audience gasps)

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:51.400
Thanks for watching!

00:03:51.409 --> 00:03:55.349
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:55.349 --> 00:03:59.469
And leave us a comment to let us know which
prediction spooked you the most...

